# =============================================================================
# Local Vector Database (Never Commit)
# =============================================================================
# Written without a trailing slash on purpose: `git check-ignore` only honours
# a trailing-slash pattern for a directory that already exists on disk, so the
# pattern must match the bare path too.
data/qdrant_storage

# =============================================================================
# Retrieval Indexes & Cached Artifacts
# =============================================================================
data/processed/index_minilm/
data/processed/index_bm25/

# Keep processed datasets (.json) under version control
#
# The negation is the point. `data/processed/*` on its own ignored exactly the
# files the comment above promised to keep, and nothing under data/processed/
# was tracked — including chunks_semantic_v2.json, the live corpus that
# src/api/config.py reads, that BM25 indexes, and whose sha256 is recorded as
# corpus_chunks_sha256 in the v2 dataset envelope. A fresh clone had no corpus:
# BM25 silently degraded to an empty index (`self._bm25` stays None, so
# `bm25_search` returns []) and every recorded baseline became unreproducible.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/*.json

# =============================================================================
# Generated Results
# =============================================================================
results/debug/
results/logs/

results/eval_phase2_results.json
results/retrieval_eval.json
results/metrics/eval_phase2_*.json

